{"id":"mahabharata-12-283","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":283,"title":"त्र्यशीत्यधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 283 · Gains rightly won","summary":{"en":"Parashara says that small gains are praised if won by the right means, such as a brahmin by gifts, and that a kshatriya by weapon, a vaishya by justice and a shudra by service. He tells how anger destroyed shame and so bewilderment arose, and how kings followed the demonic acts.","kn":"ಸರಿಯಾದ ಮಾರ್ಗದಿಂದ ಗಳಿಸಿದ ಸ್ವಲ್ಪ ಧನವೂ ಪ್ರಶಂಸಾರ್ಹ: ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣನಿಗೆ ದಾನ, ಕ್ಷತ್ರಿಯನಿಗೆ ಶಸ್ತ್ರ, ವೈಶ್ಯನಿಗೆ ನ್ಯಾಯ, ಶೂದ್ರನಿಗೆ ಸೇವೆ ಎಂದು ಪರಾಶರ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಕ್ರೋಧ ನಾಚಿಕೆಯನ್ನು ನಾಶಮಾಡಿ ಮೋಹ ಹುಟ್ಟಿತು, ರಾಜರು ಆಸುರ ಕರ್ಮಗಳನ್ನು ಅನುಸರಿಸಿದರು.","hi":"पराशर कहते हैं कि उचित साधनों से पाया थोड़ा धन भी प्रशंसनीय है, जैसे ब्राह्मण को दान, क्षत्रिय को शस्त्र, वैश्य को न्याय और शूद्र को सेवा से। वे बताते हैं कि क्रोध से लज्जा नष्ट हुई और मोह उपजा, और राजा आसुरी कर्म करने लगे।","te":"సరైన మార్గంలో సంపాదించిన కొద్ది ధనమైనా ప్రశంసనీయమని, బ్రాహ్మణునికి దానం, క్షత్రియునికి శస్త్రం, వైశ్యునికి న్యాయం, శూద్రునికి సేవ అని పరాశరుడు చెబుతాడు. కోపం సిగ్గును నాశనం చేసి మోహం పుట్టిందని, రాజులు ఆసుర కర్మలు అనుసరించారని అంటాడు.","ta":"சரியான வழியில் பெற்ற சிறு செல்வமும் போற்றத்தக்கது: அந்தணனுக்குத் தானம், க்ஷத்திரியனுக்கு ஆயுதம், வைசியனுக்கு நியாயம், சூத்திரனுக்குப் பணிவிடை என்று பராசரர் கூறுகிறார். சினம் நாணத்தை அழித்து மயக்கம் பிறந்தது, மன்னர்கள் அசுரச் செயல்களைப் பின்பற்றினர் என்கிறார்.","ml":"ശരിയായ മാർഗ്ഗത്തിലൂടെ നേടുന്ന ചെറിയ നേട്ടവും പ്രശംസിക്കപ്പെടുന്നുവെന്ന് പരാശരൻ പറയുന്നു; ദാനത്താൽ ബ്രാഹ്മണനും, ആയുധത്താൽ ക്ഷത്രിയനും, നീതിയാൽ വൈശ്യനും, സേവനത്താൽ ശൂദ്രനും നേട്ടമുണ്ടാകുന്നു. കോപം ലജ്ജയെ നശിപ്പിച്ചതും അങ്ങനെ മോഹമുണ്ടായതും, രാജാക്കന്മാർ അസുരപ്രവൃത്തികളെ പിന്തുടർന്നതും അദ്ദേഹം വിവരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.283; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"मोक्षधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Mokshadharma Parva (Duties for liberation)","verses":[{"text":"पराशर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Parashara said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"प्रतिग्रहागता विप्रे क्षत्रिये शस्त्रनिर्जिताः ।\nवैश्ये न्यायार्जिताश्चैव शूद्रे शुश्रूषयार्जिताः ।\nस्वल्पाप्यर्थाः प्रशस्यन्ते धर्मस्यार्थे महाफलाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gains that come to a Brahmin by gifts, to a Kshatriya by conquest with weapons, to a Vaishya by just earnings, and to a Shudra by service are praised, even when small, and bear great fruit for dharma."}},{"n":2,"text":"नित्यं त्रयाणां वर्णानां शूद्रः शुश्रूषुरुच्यते ।\nक्षत्रधर्मा वैश्यधर्मा नावृत्तिः पतति द्विजः ।\nशूद्रकर्मा यदा तु स्यात्तदा पतति वै द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A Shudra is said always to serve the three classes. A twice-born who lacks a livelihood does not fall by following the duty of a Kshatriya or a Vaishya; but when he takes up a Shudra's work, then the twice-born does fall."}},{"n":3,"text":"वाणिज्यं पाशुपाल्यं च तथा शिल्पोपजीवनम् ।\nशूद्रस्यापि विधीयन्ते यदा वृत्तिर्न जायते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Trade, cattle-herding and living by crafts are also allowed to a Shudra when no livelihood is to be had."}},{"n":4,"text":"रङ्गावतरणं चैव तथा रूपोपजीवनम् ।\nमद्यमांसोपजीव्यं च विक्रयो लोहचर्मणोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So too are acting on a stage and living by one's looks, living by liquor and meat, and selling iron and leather."}},{"n":5,"text":"अपूर्विणा न कर्तव्यं कर्म लोके विगर्हितम् ।\nकृतपूर्विणस्तु त्यजतो महान्धर्म इति श्रुतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who has not done a censured action before should not do it in the world; but for one who did it before and gives it up, there is great dharma, so scripture says."}},{"n":6,"text":"संसिद्धः पुरुषो लोके यदाचरति पापकम् ।\nमदेनाभिप्लुतमनास्तच्च नग्राह्यमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When a man who is perfected in the world does something sinful with a mind flooded by intoxication, that is not to be taken up."}},{"n":7,"text":"श्रूयन्ते हि पुराणे वै प्रजा धिग्दण्डशासनाः ।\nदान्ता धर्मप्रधानाश्च न्यायधर्मानुवर्तकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"For it is heard in the old tradition that the people were ruled by the penalty of reproach, self-controlled, putting dharma first, and following justice and dharma."}},{"n":8,"text":"धर्म एव सदा नॄणामिह राजन्प्रशस्यते ।\nधर्मवृद्धा गुणानेव सेवन्ते हि नरा भुवि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dharma alone is always praised for men here, king; for those grown in dharma practice only good qualities on earth."}},{"n":9,"text":"तं धर्ममसुरास्तात नामृष्यन्त जनाधिप ।\nविवर्धमानाः क्रमशस्तत्र तेऽन्वाविशन्प्रजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Asuras, dear one, lord of men, could not bear that dharma. Growing by degrees, they entered into the people there."}},{"n":10,"text":"तेषां दर्पः समभवत्प्रजानां धर्मनाशनः ।\nदर्पात्मनां ततः क्रोधः पुनस्तेषामजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Among those people arrogance arose, destroying dharma; and from that arrogance, anger arose in them again."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततः क्रोधाभिभूतानां वृत्तं लज्जासमन्वितम् ।\nह्रीश्चैवाप्यनशद्राजंस्ततो मोहो व्यजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in those overcome by anger, conduct with modesty, and shame itself, king, vanished, and then delusion was born."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो मोहपरीतास्ते नापश्यन्त यथा पुरा ।\nपरस्परावमर्देन वर्तयन्ति यथासुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, wrapped in delusion, they did not see as before and went on living as they pleased by trampling one another."}},{"n":13,"text":"तान्प्राप्य तु स धिग्दण्डो नकारणमतोऽभवत् ।\nततोऽभ्यगच्छन्देवांश्च ब्राह्मणांश्चावमन्य ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the penalty of reproach reached them, it was no longer effective; and so they went against the gods and despised the Brahmins."}},{"n":14,"text":"एतस्मिन्नेव काले तु देवा देववरं शिवम् ।\nअगच्छञ्शरणं वीरं बहुरूपं गणाधिपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At just that time the gods went for refuge to the best of gods, Shiva, the hero of many forms, lord of the hosts."}},{"n":15,"text":"तेन स्म ते गगनगाः सपुराः पातिताः क्षितौ ।\nतिस्रोऽप्येकेन बाणेन देवाप्यायिततेजसा ॥","meaning":{"en":"By him, with one arrow charged with the gods' strength, the three sky-moving cities with their dwellers were felled to the earth."}},{"n":16,"text":"तेषामधिपतिस्त्वासीद्भीमो भीमपराक्रमः ।\nदेवतानां भयकरः स हतः शूलपाणिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Their chief was a terrible one of terrible might, a source of fear to the gods, and he was slain by the one who bears the trident."}},{"n":17,"text":"तस्मिन्हतेऽथ स्वं भावं प्रत्यपद्यन्त मानवाः ।\nप्रावर्तन्त च वेदा वै शास्त्राणि च यथा पुरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he was slain, men returned to their true nature, and the Vedas and the scriptures flowed again as before."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततोऽभ्यषिञ्चन्राज्येन देवानां दिवि वासवम् ।\nसप्तर्षयश्चान्वयुञ्जन्नराणां दण्डधारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then they consecrated Indra as king of the gods in heaven, and the seven sages appointed rulers to hold the rod of punishment over men."}},{"n":19,"text":"सप्तर्षीणामथोर्ध्वं च विपृथुर्नाम पार्थिवः ।\nराजानः क्षत्रियाश्चैव मण्डलेषु पृथक्पृथक् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Above the seven sages there was a king named Vipruthu, and there were the kings and Kshatriyas in their separate territories."}},{"n":20,"text":"महाकुलेषु ये जाता वृत्ताः पूर्वतराश्च ये ।\nतेषामथासुरो भावो हृदयान्नापसर्पति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those born in great families and those who came before still have the Asura temper, which does not leave the heart."}},{"n":21,"text":"तस्मात्तेनैव भावेन सानुषङ्गेन पार्थिवाः ।\nआसुराण्येव कर्माणि न्यषेवन्भीमविक्रमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"So by that very disposition, with its attachments, the kings of terrible might followed Asura practices."}},{"n":22,"text":"प्रत्यतिष्ठंश्च तेष्वेव तान्येव स्थापयन्ति च ।\nभजन्ते तानि चाद्यापि ये बालिशतमा नराः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They took their stand on those, they establish them, and even today the most foolish of men follow them."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्मादहं ब्रवीमि त्वां राजन्संचिन्त्य शास्त्रतः ।\nसंसिद्धाधिगमं कुर्यात्कर्म हिंसात्मकं त्यजेत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So I tell you, king, after reflecting on the scriptures: one should make gains in a perfected way and give up violent action."}},{"n":24,"text":"न संकरेण द्रविणं विचिन्वीत विचक्षणः ।\nधर्मार्थं न्यायमुत्सृज्य न तत्कल्याणमुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"The discerning man should not collect wealth by mixing means; giving up justice for the sake of dharma and wealth is not called good."}},{"n":25,"text":"स त्वमेवंविधो दान्तः क्षत्रियः प्रियबान्धवः ।\nप्रजा भृत्यांश्च पुत्रांश्च स्वधर्मेणानुपालय ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, such as you are, self-controlled, a Kshatriya dear to your kin, protect your subjects, dependents and sons by your own dharma."}},{"n":26,"text":"इष्टानिष्टसमायोगो वैरं सौहार्दमेव च ।\nअथ जातिसहस्राणि बहूनि परिवर्तते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting with the loved and the unloved, enmity and friendship: the soul passes through many thousands of births."}},{"n":27,"text":"तस्माद्गुणेषु रज्येथा मा दोषेषु कदाचन ।\nनिर्गुणो यो हि दुर्बुद्धिरात्मनः सोऽरिरुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So take delight in good qualities and never in faults; for the ill-minded man without good qualities is called his own enemy."}},{"n":28,"text":"मानुषेषु महाराज धर्माधर्मौ प्रवर्ततः ।\nन तथान्येषु भूतेषु मनुष्यरहितेष्विह ॥","meaning":{"en":"In human beings, great king, dharma and adharma are at work; not so among other creatures here without humans."}},{"n":29,"text":"धर्मशीलो नरो विद्वानीहकोऽनीहकोऽपि वा ।\nआत्मभूतः सदा लोके चरेद्भूतान्यहिंसयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man of dharma, learned, whether he acts for ends or not, should always move through the world regarding beings as himself, harming none."}},{"n":30,"text":"यदा व्यपेतहृल्लेखं मनो भवति तस्य वै ।\nनानृतं चैव भवति तदा कल्याणमृच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"When his mind becomes free of inner stain, then he is without falsehood and gains well-being."}}]}]}